+# Stage directions in m02 to m07: what changed
+
+Voiced lines now hold only spoken words (tts-audio rule 7, user, 2026-11-10). Every inline cue such as `*quietly*` in a voiced line of missions m02 to m07 was taken out of the text. The lead list was `STAGE_DIRECTIONS_AUDIT.md`; every hit was checked by hand, and a fresh scan of all `scenarios/m0[2-7]_*/ink/*.ink` (asterisk cues, bracketed and parenthesised directions, including lines inside `{...}` blocks, which the audit skipped) found nothing it had missed. The voice-tag branch's `dialoguelint.mjs` (`inline-direction` rule) now reports none for these six missions. Emphasis (`*really*`) did not occur in these missions.
+
+## How each cue was handled
+
+- **Delivery note.** A cue inside a person-chat line was removed and became a `#delivery:` tag at the end of the line (syntax and limits from `TtsService::DELIVERY_TAG` on `build/voice-direction-tag`: one note, under 200 characters, last one wins). The note is written for the voice: pace, volume, mood. Pure movement cues were turned into a note only where they shape the delivery ("pointing something out", "not looking up").
+- **Narrator line.** Three cues were physical beats the scene would lose: Sister Doyle looking round for the first time (the README's own example of a scene turn), Irina holding out her wrists, and Kemal pocketing his watch before the fight. Each is now a short third person, present tense narrator line just above the spoken line, written the way that file already writes narration (inline `Narrator:` in the ward nurse file; `#speaker:narrator`, then the NPC's `#speaker:` restored, in the Irina and minder files). Each narrator line sits above the knot's or choice's tags and assignments, so no tag moved to a different line.
+- **Phone.** Ghost's lines in `m02_phone_ghost.ink` are a voiced video call (`npcType: phone`), which sends no delivery note, so the cue was removed and nothing added.
+
+Nothing else changed: same words, same line order, no logic, choices, diverts or other tags touched. `tagdiff.mjs --ref 1f959061d` over the six missions shows only the added `#delivery:` tags and the two `#speaker:narrator` tags.
+
+## Counts
+
+| Mission | Lines changed | Delivery tags | Narrator lines added | Cues removed with no tag (phone) | Old text had a clip | Lines to voice |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| m02 | 40 | 33 | 1 | 6 | 34 | 41 |
+| m03 | 9 | 9 | 0 | 0 | 9 | 9 |
