+| m07 | 2 | 2 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 2 |
+| **Total** | **73** | **64** | **3** | **6** | **43** | **76** |
+
+"Lines to voice" counts every changed line plus each new narrator line (m02 and m03 voice their narration, so m02's new narrator line needs a clip; m04 to m07 have no audio yet). A delivery note is part of the line's cache key, so a tagged line needs a new clip even where its words were already voiced. Voltage's `m04_npc_voltage.ink:507` is a sequence, so its one line is two clips. No audio was generated and no clip was deleted; the 43 old clips (34 in m02, 9 in m03) are now orphans for `tts:wasted` to list once the new lines are voiced.
+
+## Checks
+
+For each mission: `scripts/compile-ink.sh <mission>` (no failures), `dialoguelint.mjs` totals identical to before the change (and no `inline-direction` warning with the voice-tag branch's lint), and the validator (`--no-graph`) run on the old and new ink with an identical list of errors and warnings.
+
+## Build log
+
+2026-11-10, branch `build/stage-directions-m02-m07` from `claude/break-escape-access-design-090sjx` (`1f959061d`). One commit per mission (m02, m03, m04, m05, m07, m06) and one for these docs. Judgement calls, for the user to overrule: the three narrator lines above (the rest of the movement cues became notes, since the words or the item hand-over already carry them); Gary's keycard hand-over (`*a pause, then he holds it out*`) and Irina's badge (`*unclips it*`) stayed as notes because `#give_item` already shows the hand-over; m02's narrator line will be voiced in the narrator voice, as the mission's other narration is. The `#delivery:` tag only reaches the voice once `build/voice-direction-tag` is merged; until then the engine ignores it and the line plays its plain text.
